{"type":"standard","title":"Darline Graham","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Darline Graham</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q140537772","titles":{"canonical":"Darline_Graham","normalized":"Darline Graham","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Darline Graham</span></span>"},"pageid":83683581,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Official_portrait_of_Darline_Graham%2C_member_of_the_United_States_Senate_from_South_Carolina_%282026%29.jpg/330px-Official_portrait_of_Darline_Graham%2C_member_of_the_United_States_Senate_from_South_Carolina_%282026%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Official_portrait_of_Darline_Graham%2C_member_of_the_United_States_Senate_from_South_Carolina_%282026%29.jpg/3840px-Official_portrait_of_Darline_Graham%2C_member_of_the_United_States_Senate_from_South_Carolina_%282026%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":4312,"height":5389},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377353223","tid":"c1c45ca5-bba7-11f1-986f-ba9f61133d4c","timestamp":"2026-09-29T01:47:41Z","description":"American politician (born 1964)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darline_Graham","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darline_Graham?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darline_Graham?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Darline_Graham"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darline_Graham","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Darline_Graham","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darline_Graham?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Darline_Graham"}},"extract":"Darline Lettie Graham Nordone is an American politician and public administrator serving as the junior United States senator from South Carolina, a seat she has held since July 14, 2026. A member of the Republican Party, she was appointed to fill the vacancy created by the death of her older brother, Lindsey Graham. She is the first woman to represent South Carolina in the United States Senate.","extract_html":"<p><b>Darline Lettie Graham Nordone</b> is an American politician and public administrator serving as the junior United States senator from South Carolina, a seat she has held since July 14, 2026. A member of the Republican Party, she was appointed to fill the vacancy created by the death of her older brother, Lindsey Graham. She is the first woman to represent South Carolina in the United States Senate.</p>"}